Stable rest uses the game's existing one-health-per-six-hours rule. It requires
conscious, uncaptured people with no bleeding. The recovery bound comes from
their actual wounds. The recovery preserves ammunition, dressing counts and
earlier deaths. Its treasury is exactly 64,692 + 19 × 8,000 − 8,568 pesos;
the paid time and renewals remain part of the campaign.

Hourly mechanical work restores actual wear using finite materials. It does not
clear an ignition failure. A loaded jammed gun receives an ordinary paid reprime
before departure, preserving its ammunition. Collection can advance the clock,
so a repair worker and target are selected again from their current condition.

The optional old commander top-up before northern body discovery was removed.
That approach now retains his actual worn weapon and equipment. It does not
require perfect condition or a free repair.

## Remaining acceptance

The fresh uncached run passes Córdoba and its subsequent defense. A scoped
continuation from that earned official save now passes recovery, a second real
defense and Tucumán. Its relief plan exposed two separate test-helper errors:
the cache approach chose a roof coordinate above a ground chest, and the courier
requested twenty extra dressings despite already owning eighteen. The corrected
ground approach passes actual collection and four focused checks. The delivery
now uses twenty owned dressings in total, including a real two-dressing donation
from Quiroga. Córdoba's existing gun reaches Tucumán with its loaded charge and
six reserves unchanged.

The relief plan now explicitly renews its intended supporters during the nested
gun transport waits. A focused three-gun test proves actual paid extensions for
a named remote reserve, exact expiry seconds, unchanged health and charges,
normal expiry when retention is omitted, and deterministic saved replay.

The first Salta tactic wins but loses the three provincial officers. The
existing cautious tactic wins a shorter battle and keeps Quiroga and Azurduy
alive, while Paz remains dead. It leaves ten actual survivors in Salta, all
stable; Quiroga retains his real fifteen-health wound. An earlier helper forced
Paz to carry the agreement. Yatasto's public mission rules accept
an actual capable speaker in Tucumán through ordinary observed adjacent
conversations. They do not require actor eleven. The corrected mission helper
selects Azurduy, checks every actual acute survivor before waits and retains
serving paid contracts at their exact expiry seconds. This accepted checkpoint
has no bleeding, so it needs no aid or new equipment. The generalized acute-care
branch received a source review but has not been exercised by this checkpoint.
These scoped results do not replace a fresh run of the whole final candidate.

The unchanged scoped Cuyo continuation from the earned Yatasto save passes
finite hospital care and two actual gun shipments. It stops before Mendoza:
actor 101 lacks three musket rounds for the helper's twelve-round target. This
is an actual finite shortage after the available depot, known loot and cache
paths are exhausted. The failed attempt emitted no full failure-state save;
its numeric reports do not establish an accepted Cuyo checkpoint.

Read-only state reports then preserve the actual assembly and pre-ammunition
checkpoint. The old rearm step converts useful native pistols and shotguns to
muskets without matching that force to finite ammunition. The stock-only plan
retains native guns and the existing twelve-round target for all 27 soldiers.
Actual off-family carried pistol rounds enter the local depot through ordinary
store orders. Courier Güemes makes a four-hour trip each way and collects
12 + 12 + 3 musket rounds from known Tucumán bodies, leaving twenty of the
original forty-seven. He returns and stores those actual rounds. The 29 loaded
charges in unused local guns and both recovered bronze pieces remain intact.

The scoped preparation passes on the original gameplay source and creates an
official paired Mendoza assault save. Fifteen paid renewals retain exact
expiry seconds and cost 9,217 pesos. Its treasury is exactly
385,793 + 8,000 port income − 9,217 renewals − 20 courier travel − 50 assault
approaches = 384,506 pesos. Immediate queued orders report no debit; the actual
posta fee is paid during journey advancement. Health, native gun/load metadata,
condition, dressings and non-ammunition equipment remain unchanged. Independent
source and saved-state review pass. This proves preparation only.

The exact prepared assault then runs on main's merged roof-defense source.
Ordinary entry equals the saved initial battle; the existing battery controller
wins in eleven turns with 609 actions and 115 actual seconds. All 651 recorded
orders replay, the terminal battle/campaign pair passes official save validation,
and settlement adds the ordinary 250-peso victory payment. No army, health,
cartridges, seeds or successful outcomes are recreated or assigned.

The seven new deployed soldier deaths are 136, 119, 103, 140, 113, 141 and 8.
An accidental actual shot by 108 also kills Barcala (7). This is eight
new campaign deaths, not seven; all sixteen earlier casualties persist. Twenty
deployed soldiers survive and none is captured. The physical ammunition ledger
retains 280 rounds on people and bodies and six in original dropped guns, from
324 before combat: 38 actual charges were consumed. Nine paid dressing strokes
spend nine of the 48 carried dressings. Eight actual bronze-gun shots leave
both pieces loaded, with three and one reserve charges respectively.

Five actual survivors remain acute after settlement. Mendoza patients 122 and
129 have 8 and 7 health with four bleeding each. Routed survivors 127, 144 and
9 are in neutral `cell-6-24`, with 20/16/53 health and 4/4/2 bleeding. Strategic
care is unavailable in that neutral cell; its three people carry only one
dressing. Finite local aid or lawful travel must resolve all five before a
global recovery or funding wait is accepted.

A separate first care trial chooses medic 146 for local patients 122 and 129.
His ordinary nineteen-cell approach takes 59 seconds. Both patients die from
their actual bleeding before the dressing can be applied. The doctor still
owns both dressings; cash and firearm seed are unchanged. The four accepted
orders replay and the official active pair retains both deaths at hour 1,426,
second 1,921. Its return settlement is pending. This failed care branch does
not establish recovery or replace the immutable Mendoza settlement above.
The rural survivors have not been visited or treated in this trial.

The accepted alternative starts from the immutable Mendoza settlement. Doctors
146 and 107 spend one real medical-assignment hour and two owned dressings to
stop the two local critical bleeds before any tactical approach. The three
rural patients lose one actual health each during that hour. The doctor then
collects four of the six known dressings on body 136 through ordinary field
orders. Two local and three rural manual strokes cost 100 clinical action
points and five dressings. Reaching the rural patients uses Mendoza's actual
northern boundary; no location, control or patient is assigned.

This alternative ends at hour 1,427, second 2,039 after one hour and 178 field
seconds. Patients 122/129/127/144/9 have 15/15/19/15/50 health and no bleeding;
Quiroga's additional two-point field loss remains. Living dressing stock falls
from 29 to 26 and body 136 from six to two: the combined stock spends exactly
seven. All 24 prior deaths, contracts, nonmedical gear, firearm ammunition and
gun records remain exact. The complete 24-order replay and official saves pass
after lossless expansion of the saved cell scene. This scoped result does not
establish full recovery or the later campaign.

The reusable stock-only helper then derives its doctor and finite supply
choices from that same immutable settlement. It completes 32 ordinary orders
at hour 1,427, second 2,037 with the same five final health and bleeding values,
the same cash and the same seven-dressing clinical cost. Doctors 146 and 139
provide the actual hourly work. The courier collects four existing dressings
from two known enemy sources and body 136. A complete saved-order replay and
a second complete helper execution agree; every tactical order also agrees
with the presented executor. The helper preserves all 24 prior deaths and the
actual contracts, firearm ammunition and nonmedical equipment. This separate
receipt verifies the reusable policy; it does not replace the earlier distinct
care trials or prove a fresh full campaign on the final working candidate.
After independent review, accepted orders are recorded before the post-action
safety check, so an interrupted run retains its final valid action. The full
successful helper proof passes again with that reporting correction.
An independent interruption control uses a separately declared threat fixture,
not an earned campaign raid. Before official initial admission it launches the
canonical sixteen-person group, debits eighteen enemy reserves to two and
declares arrival at hour 1,427. The helper's fifth accepted order is a real
one-hour wait: it consumes two owned dressings and raises an actual pending
encounter. The helper stops, and its complete five-order saved replay matches
the reported stopped pair. Both its reported and physical hourly consumption
equal two after the receipt fix. The original earned settlement is unchanged.

The public campaign requires living engineer Beltrán (2) and commander San
Martín (57), not Barcala. Both remain alive. The test route's fixed Barcala
foundry recruiter and trainer choices now use actual eligible surviving
leaders. The scoped foundry continuation selects actual delegates in Mendoza,
meets Beltrán and pays the ordinary 650 pesos for the two projects. Beltrán
joins with his actual 76 health; Barcala stays dead and unrecruited. The helper's
deliberate release of costly specialist 142 returns his exact rifle and loaded
charge, ten spare rounds, bayonet, clothing and carried supplies to the local
service-return inventory. The two recovered gun records remain unchanged.
Official save and deterministic function replay pass at hour 1,427, second
2,128, with 384,106 pesos. This does not prove training, army funding, the
mountain column or the ending.

The same foundry helper also passes independently from the reusable care
helper's accepted save. It ends at hour 1,427, second 2,064 with 384,106 pesos,
the actual living engineer, dead Barcala, all 24 prior deaths and the same exact
specialist property return. Official save and complete function replay agree.
These two foundry receipts retain their distinct medical predecessors.

A read-only audit found fixed-person mountain-helper assumptions. The working
helpers now select actual capable leaders, eight issued soldiers, two qualified
doctors and a distinct finite dressing donor. They transfer only the doctors'
actual deficits and retain the intended force through exact expiry seconds.
Four declared Los Patos deployment scenarios verify finite transfers and exact
tactical saved replay. They do not establish an earned mountain deployment,
campaign save replay or victory. The Uspallata and Los Patos journey branches
remain unexercised on the ordinary stock route below.

The next bounded preparation starts from the reusable-care foundry save at
hour 1,427, second 2,064 and 384,106 pesos. It uses the integrated working source
identity `f28f0f90bd896`; this is not a new production-build claim. Twenty-seven
actual medical hours spend 27 existing dressings and restore the four wounded
Mendoza patients to their actual maximum health. The three stable rural
survivors keep their existing health. All 20 serving survivors remain alive
and free; all 24 earlier deaths persist. Four exact-second renewals cost 516
pesos. A real Córdoba course costs 60 pesos and trains three militia; posta
travel costs 20 pesos. Three ordinary port payments add 24,000 pesos, leaving
384,106 + 24,000 − 516 − 60 − 20 = 407,510 pesos.

Preparation then stops at a real third-gun shortage. Two controlled bronze
pieces are stored in Mendoza: `arsenal:cordoba:2` and
`arsenal:buenos_aires:1`, still loaded with three and one reserve charges.
The third piece, `arsenal:cordoba:1`, remains physically in Salta, loaded with
six reserves. Salta is royalist, so the gun is excluded from controlled
recovery. The Buenos Aires and Córdoba arsenals have already been claimed;
neither provides another gun. The helper does not lower the three-piece
requirement, grant a replacement or report funding. Its official stopped save
and complete deterministic stopped-function replay agree at hour 1,488,
second 2,064. Lawful recapture or recovery remains necessary. No mountain
battle or funded army is established by this receipt.

One bounded recapture continuation starts from that immutable stopped save.
It uses the same source identity `f28f0f90bd896` and freezes all 880 test and
support files, with digest `c23d5fff9445c90b91fb2f285cb3bf29a0b916e432ab7a438b6b5f4e623b2f99`.
Six actual weekly hires are 105, 128, 145, 109, 135 and 147. They cost
335,580 pesos and complete their six-hour arrivals. Six actual local supporters
are 1, 117, 100, 107, 116 and 130. Two rural renewals cost 258 pesos; the two
squads' posta travel costs 40 pesos; one ordinary port payment adds 8,000 pesos.
The owned `arsenal:cordoba:2` travels from Mendoza to Córdoba, then enters the
daylight assault loaded with three reserve charges. The unused Buenos Aires
gun stays in Mendoza, loaded with one reserve. All 97 accepted preparation
orders replay and official saves agree at hour 1,520, second 2,064. No source,
test, health, gear, ammunition, seed or outcome is changed during the proof.

The actual battle wins in fourteen turns, with 357 tactical actions and 111
seconds. Operatives 1, 100, 107, 135 and 147 die. All 24 prior deaths persist.
Four actual gun fires consume the loaded charge and three reserves; seven
accepted partial reload orders leave the gun unloaded with zero reserve.
Three ordinary self-dressing actions consume carried dressings. Operative 145
legally receives one musket round from 117, then recovers and equips a dropped
1800 weapon. Every ordinary and presented tactical result agrees; official
per-action saves and the complete preparation, battle and settlement replay
pass. The input save, source and all frozen test files remain unchanged.

Quiet settlement ends at hour 1,520, second 2,175 with Tucumán patriot,
21 living soldiers, 29 dead, and no pending battle or encounter. Cash is exactly
407,510 − 335,580 − 258 − 40 + 8,000 + 250 = 79,882 pesos. Routed survivors
116 and 117 are in Córdoba with 20 and 44 health and three bleeding each.
No subsequent care or time is included in this receipt. Rural survivors 127,
144, 9 and 146 remain stable with their existing health; all 21 serving
survivors retain their actual unexpired terms. Rural 127 and 144 next expire
at hour 1,523, seconds 1,255 and 1,940. Salta recovery, the third gun, army
funding and both mountain battles remain open.

The next distinct aid receipt starts from the immutable recapture settlement.
It selects the actual Córdoba squad, assembles only local 0, 116 and 117, and
visits the unchanged saved scene. The existing aid planner's ordinary prefix
equips each bleeding survivor's medical hand and applies one real self-care
stroke. Eight accepted orders take six seconds. Each native dressing count
falls from two to one; health stays 20 and 44 while both bleeds stop. Ordinary
return admits the quiet official save at hour 1,520, second 2,181, still with
79,882 pesos. No hourly wait, renewal, supply trip, new scene, hire or Salta
action occurs. All 29 deaths, all 21 serving people, gun records, ammunition,
condition and clothing remain exact. Per-action official saves, complete
campaign/tactical/return replay and ordinary/presented execution agree. The
immutable input, the same source identity and all frozen test files remain
unchanged. This proves stabilization, not full healing or the mountain route.

Five focused helper integration checks also pass on this working test tree.
Three declared paid-service cases cover exact expiry, finite critical care,
and reporting the final accepted action before an interrupted route stops.
Two declared mountain-care cases cover successful finite dressings and a
physical obstruction that leaves actual untreated patients in a saved battle.
Each checks official saves, deterministic replay and unchanged input. These
declared encounters do not establish an earned mountain journey or victory,
and do not replace the complete short suite required before publication.

Cuyo, all thirteen controlled localities, saved victory
and the subsequent 48 hours of actual service expiry and agreed port payments
remain unproved. A coastal or recovery checkpoint does not establish the full
ending.

Before the subsequent mission-helper edits, the complete short suite passed
4,884 checks across all 700 selected files, with no failures or skips. The final
unchanged candidate must pass again before publication. The independent
eight-file helper batch was merged in [PR #164](https://github.com/fsodano/granaderos/pull/164).
Its complete short suite passed 4,884/4,884 tests across 700/700 files with no
failures, cancellations or skips. The tested and merged tree is
`e6bcae961c602935280f5ed9cd450fdda99fae9d`; merge commit
`e4147b09e6f251d0c92ae1dbdc6fcd7683914aa1`. That batch does not contain the
broader stock-ending fixtures or establish the full ending. Cannon and map
presentation remain with the separate 3D work.
The subsequent [PR #165](https://github.com/fsodano/granaderos/pull/165) corrects
guerrilla defense to use the occupied surface's cover. Its complete short suite
passes 4,885/4,885 checks across 700/700 files, with no failures or skips; the
tested and merged tree is `f26ca1d40d099b9dcb60346ecfa4c37c5921b545`, merge
`ad4098fdcd5ba26b7c1d48d819b0dbf9039e41c4`. Its affected, type, production-build
and audit gates pass. Those results cover that isolated batch, not the later
working stock fixtures or the full ordinary campaign.
The subsequent [PR #166](https://github.com/fsodano/granaderos/pull/166) adds the
optional enclosed-room fear ability. Its 147 affected checks and complete
4,895/4,895 short checks across 702/702 files pass, with no failures or skips.
The tested and merged tree is `b6ff92395c3c07b2b7d3590a9826fa18a2b09e56`, merge
`b87e09319eedc733cf97c8b2210030e25a0b80b5`. Paid declared ground and upper-room
arenas establish the ability, finite actions and saved replay; they do not
establish conquest or the stock ending. The scoped stock receipts above used
their stated earlier sources and are not a fresh campaign on this later merge.
Full-video acceptance, wider personality behavior, quest choices and physical
model refinement remain open in the [video requirements](ja2-video-review-2026-10-03.md).
